:href "/events/321000"} "56 from 41 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "This was the first event to finish at the London 2012 Olympics. The favorite was China’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/122169"} "Yi Siling"] " and she showed why by winning the gold medal. However it was a close battle with Poland’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/104737"} "Sylwia Bogacka"] ", but Yi won with her last three shots of 10.7, 10.3 and 10.5. Yi’s teammate " [:a {:href "/athletes/122170"} "Yu Dan"] " gave China two medals in the event with her bronze. The defending champion, Czech shooter " [:a {:href "/athletes/104664"} "Kateřína Emmons"] " almost did not qualify for the final, but made it as the last qualifier in a shoot-off, with five shooters contesting four spots. She had a solid final round to move up to fourth place but could not catch Yu, who also outshot her in the final round. Russian " [:a {:href "/athletes/124270"} "Darya Vdovina"] " was equal third after the qualifier but struggled in the final and finished eighth."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Malaysian " [:a {:href "/athletes/126293"} "Nur Suryani Mohd Taibi"] " placed 34th of 56 shooters, but did so while she was eight-months pregnant. While there are 14 known Olympians to have competed while pregnant, nobody was as close to term as Mohd Taibi."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "Qualifying Shoot-Off 5-9"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1164"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/122169"} "Yi Siling"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CHN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CHN.png"}] "CHN"]] [:td {} "399 (2)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "502.9 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} 